{
  "configuration_id": "config_016",
  "reason": "Evidence: Only one experiment (config_001: rna_only, singleprofile, pca_n2000) is complete, yielding ~48.5% accuracy and ~46.4% F1, establishing a weak RNA-only baseline. The largest unresolved design question is whether adding image information provides complementary signal. Question tested: config_016 (multimodal, singleprofile, pca_n2000, resnet50, concat) is the minimal-change extension of config_001—identical RNA encoder and profile setting, with only the addition of a ResNet50 image branch and simple concat fusion. This isolates the effect of the image modality. Why this is the best next experiment: (1) model_setting (unimodal vs. multimodal) is the highest-level design decision; resolving it can eliminate or prioritize ~36 of the remaining 50 configs. (2) It is a clean A/B comparison to config_001, changing only the addition of image, so any performance difference can be attributed to the image branch. (3) If multimodal significantly outperforms RNA-only, it justifies investing remaining budget in multimodal variants (better encoders, aggregation, fusion). If it does not, the search can focus on improving the RNA representation (scvi, scgpt) or profile/aggregation strategies within the unimodal space, avoiding wasted experiments on a modality that adds no value."
}

